"TENTH FIELD CIRCUIT\nEvent Privacy Notice\nVersion: 1.0\nLast updated: 15 September 2026\nEvent date: 24 October 2026\n\nThis Event Privacy Notice explains how Tenth Athletic Limited collects, uses, shares and protects personal information in connection with TENTH FIELD CIRCUIT (the “Event”), including the Individual Field and Community Field Relay.\n\nIt applies to participants, relay team members and captains, prospective participants, emergency contacts, volunteers and anyone who communicates with us about the Event.\n\nThis notice should be read together with our general Privacy & Cookie Policy and the Event Entry Terms.\n\n1. Who we are\n   Tenth Athletic Limited is the organiser of TENTH FIELD CIRCUIT and is responsible for deciding how personal information is used for the organisation and delivery of the Event.\n\nLegal company name: Tenth Athletic Limited\nCompany number: 16848676\nRegistered in: England and Wales\nPrivacy contact: info@tenthathletic.com\n\nIn this notice, “TENTH”, “we”, “us” and “our” refer to Tenth Athletic Limited.\n\n2. Registration through Let’s Do This\n   Event registration is provided through the Let’s Do This platform.\n\nLet’s Do This processes certain participant information on our behalf where it provides registration and event-management services to us. It may also process information for its own platform, account, payment, analytics and marketing purposes.\n\nWhere Let’s Do This determines how and why it uses personal information for its own purposes, it is separately responsible for that processing. You should also read the Let’s Do This Privacy Policy.\n\nWe receive from Let’s Do This the information reasonably required to administer your entry and deliver the Event. We do not normally receive your complete payment-card details.\n\n3. Information we may collect\n   Depending on how you interact with the Event, we may collect the following categories of personal information.\n\nIdentity and contact information\nThis may include:\n\nFull name;\n\nEmail address;\n\nTelephone number;\n\nPostal address, where required;\n\nDate of birth or confirmation that you are aged 18 or over;\n\nGender or competition category, where relevant;\n\nRunning club or community affiliation; and\n\nEmergency-contact details.\n\nRegistration and transaction information\nThis may include:\n\nYour chosen race format;\n\nRelay team name, team members and team captain;\n\nEntry date and registration status;\n\nEntry-fee and payment confirmation;\n\nDiscounts or promotional codes;\n\nCancellation, transfer or other entry requests; and\n\nCommunications relating to your booking.\n\nWe do not normally hold complete card numbers, card security codes or online-banking credentials. These are handled by Let’s Do This and its appointed payment providers.\n\nParticipation and performance information\nThis may include:\n\nRace number or bib number;\n\nCheck-in and attendance status;\n\nStart wave or allocated start time;\n\nTiming-chip information;\n\nSplit and finishing times;\n\nFinishing position and category ranking;\n\nRelay team results;\n\nCourse incidents;\n\nPenalties, rule breaches or disqualification decisions; and\n\nInformation required to investigate or correct a result.\n\nHealth, medical and accessibility information\nWhere necessary, we may collect information concerning:\n\nMedical conditions relevant to safe participation;\n\nAllergies;\n\nDisabilities or accessibility requirements;\n\nMedication or other information required in an emergency; and\n\nMedical assistance or incidents occurring during the Event.\n\nHealth and disability information may constitute special-category personal data and receives additional protection under data-protection law.\n\nPlease provide only information that is relevant to your safe participation or an adjustment you require.\n\nCommunications and incident information\nThis may include correspondence, enquiries, complaints, feedback, witness accounts, accident reports, insurance information and records of communications with the Event team.\n\nPhotography and recordings\nOfficial photographers, videographers and media personnel may capture photographs, video and audio at the Event. These recordings may include your image, voice, race number and participation in the Event.\n\n4. How we obtain information\n   We may obtain personal information:\n\nDirectly from you;\n\nFrom a relay team captain or another person making a permitted registration on your behalf;\n\nFrom Let’s Do This;\n\nFrom our timing and results provider;\n\nFrom event officials, marshals, medical personnel and venue staff;\n\nFrom photographers and videographers;\n\nFrom insurers, professional advisers or public authorities where appropriate; and\n\nFrom publicly available sources where reasonably necessary to administer or protect the Event.\n\nIf you provide another person’s details, including those of an emergency contact or relay team member, you must inform them that you have done so and direct them to this notice.\n\n5. How and why we use your information\n   We use personal information only where we have an appropriate lawful basis.\n\nPurpose\tInformation used\tLawful basis\nProcessing and administering your registration\tIdentity, contact, registration and transaction information\tPerformance of our contract with you\nConfirming eligibility and assigning race categories, teams, bibs and start waves\tIdentity, registration and participation information\tPerformance of our contract and our legitimate interests in operating a fair event\nCollecting entry fees and maintaining accounting records\tIdentity and transaction information\tPerformance of our contract and compliance with legal obligations\nSending essential event information, safety notices and operational updates\tIdentity and contact information\tPerformance of our contract\nTiming the Event and calculating results and rankings\tIdentity and performance information\tPerformance of our contract and our legitimate interests in producing accurate results\nPublishing results and maintaining a historical sporting record\tIdentity and performance information\tOur legitimate interests in administering, reporting and documenting the Event\nManaging safety, accessibility and medical arrangements\tIdentity, contact, health and accessibility information\tPerformance of our contract, our legitimate interests in delivering a safe event and, where required, explicit consent\nResponding to a medical emergency\tIdentity, health and emergency-contact information\tProtection of your vital interests or those of another person\nInvestigating incidents, complaints, rule breaches and insurance claims\tIdentity, communication, health and incident information\tOur legitimate interests, legal obligations and the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims\nPhotographing, filming and reporting the Event\tIdentity, participation information, photographs and recordings\tOur legitimate interests in documenting and promoting the Event and the TENTH brand\nSending optional promotional communications\tIdentity, contact and marketing-preference information\tYour consent, or another basis permitted by direct-marketing law\nProducing anonymous attendance, performance and operational statistics\tAggregated or anonymised information\tOur legitimate interests in evaluating and improving the Event\nWhere information is required to register or participate, failure to provide it may mean that we cannot accept or administer your entry.\n\n6. Health and special-category information\n   Where we ask you to provide health, medical, disability or accessibility information, we will collect only what is reasonably necessary for safety, emergency response or requested adjustments.\n\nWhere we rely on explicit consent, the registration process will ask for a separate, affirmative confirmation covering the relevant information and purposes. You may withdraw that consent by contacting info@tenthathletic.com.\n\nWithdrawing consent does not affect processing that took place before withdrawal. It may affect our ability to retain information about an adjustment or medical arrangement you requested. We will explain any practical consequences when you contact us.\n\nIn an emergency, relevant information may be shared with first-aid providers, medical professionals or emergency services where necessary to protect life or health.\n\n7. Race timing and published results\n   Event results may be published online or supplied to a timing provider, governing body, media organisation or results archive.\n\nPublished results may include:\n\nYour name;\n\nRace number;\n\nRace format or relay team;\n\nRunning club or community affiliation;\n\nAge or competition category;\n\nSplit and finishing times;\n\nFinishing position; and\n\nAny penalty or disqualification affecting the result.\n\nWe will not publish your date of birth, contact details, emergency-contact information or medical information as part of the results.\n\nResults may remain publicly available as a permanent sporting record. You may contact us if you believe a result is inaccurate or if you have a particular privacy or safety concern. Requests will be considered individually, taking account of your rights and our legitimate interest in maintaining an accurate event record.\n\n8. Photography, video and audio\n   TENTH FIELD CIRCUIT is a public sporting event at which photography, filming and audio recording may take place.\n\nWe may use event recordings for:\n\nEvent reporting and results coverage;\n\nTENTH websites and social-media channels;\n\nEditorial and documentary content;\n\nPress and public-relations activity;\n\nFuture promotion of TENTH events; and\n\nInternal training and event review.\n\nIf you have a specific safety, privacy or safeguarding concern about identifiable photography, contact info@tenthathletic.com before the Event and speak to the registration team when you arrive. We will make reasonable efforts to accommodate appropriate requests.\n\nHowever, we may not be able to prevent your incidental appearance in crowd scenes, background footage, start and finish-line coverage or recordings made by spectators and independent media.\n\nWe will seek additional permission where appropriate before using an identifiable participant as the principal subject of a testimonial or dedicated commercial campaign unrelated to general Event coverage.\n\n9. Who we may share information with\n   Where reasonably necessary, we may share relevant information with:\n\nLet’s Do This;\n\nOur appointed payment providers;\n\nTiming, tracking and results providers;\n\nLee Valley VeloPark and the relevant venue operator;\n\nRace officials, marshals and event-production contractors;\n\nFirst-aid providers, medical professionals and emergency services;\n\nSecurity, health-and-safety and incident-management providers;\n\nPhotographers, videographers, media and content-production providers;\n\nIT, hosting, email, communications and cloud-service providers;\n\nInsurers, accountants, solicitors and other professional advisers;\n\nA charity or fundraising platform, where you choose to participate in an associated fundraising activity;\n\nGoverning bodies or permit authorities where required;\n\nPolice, regulators, courts or other public authorities where required by law; and\n\nA purchaser, successor or adviser involved in a genuine business restructuring, subject to appropriate confidentiality safeguards.\n\nWe require service providers acting on our behalf to process information only for authorised purposes and to apply appropriate security measures.\n\nWe do not sell participant medical information or contact details.\n\n10. International transfers\n    Some service providers, including companies involved in the operation of Let’s Do This, may process information outside the United Kingdom.\n\nWhere personal information is transferred internationally, we will take reasonable steps to ensure that an appropriate legal safeguard applies. This may include a UK adequacy regulation, the UK International Data Transfer Agreement, the UK Addendum to approved standard contractual clauses, or another safeguard permitted by law.\n\nLet’s Do This separately explains its international processing in its own privacy policy.\n\n11. How long we keep information\n    We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the relevant purpose.\n\nOur normal retention approach is:\n\nRegistration, transaction and essential event communications: up to six years after the Event where required for accounting, contractual or legal-claims purposes;\n\nHealth, accessibility and emergency-contact information: normally deleted or anonymised within 90 days after the Event, unless connected to an incident, complaint, insurance matter or legal claim;\n\nAccident, medical-incident and insurance records: up to six years after the matter is concluded, or longer where required by law;\n\nTiming and published results: retained as a long-term or permanent sporting record;\n\nUnpublished photography and video working files: normally reviewed and deleted when no longer required for production;\n\nSelected published photographs, videos and historical Event material: retained while they continue to serve a legitimate editorial, promotional or archival purpose and reviewed periodically;\n\nGeneral enquiries and complaints: normally up to two years after the enquiry is closed, unless a longer period is necessary;\n\nMarketing information: until you opt out or the information is no longer required, after which we may retain a minimal suppression record to ensure that we respect your preference; and\n\nAnonymous statistics: may be retained indefinitely because they no longer identify an individual.\n\nWe may retain information for longer where required by law, a regulator, an insurer or the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.\n\n12. Marketing communications\n    Registration for the Event does not automatically require you to receive general TENTH marketing.\n\nWhere marketing consent is required, it will be requested separately from acceptance of the Event Entry Terms and acknowledgement of this notice.\n\nEssential messages about your registration, safety, race-day arrangements, route changes, cancellation or results are service communications and may still be sent even if you have opted out of marketing.\n\nYou may unsubscribe from marketing at any time by using the unsubscribe link in an email or contacting info@tenthathletic.com.\n\n13. Security\n    We use appropriate organisational and technical measures designed to protect personal information against accidental loss, unauthorised access, misuse, alteration or disclosure.\n\nAccess to sensitive Event information is limited to personnel and providers who reasonably need it for their role. No online system can be guaranteed to be completely secure, but we review our safeguards in proportion to the nature and sensitivity of the information involved.\n\n14. Your data-protection rights\n    Depending on the circumstances, you may have the right to:\n\nRequest access to your personal information;\n\nAsk us to correct inaccurate or incomplete information;\n\nAsk us to delete certain information;\n\nAsk us to restrict how certain information is used;\n\nObject to processing based on legitimate interests;\n\nReceive certain information in a portable format;\n\nWithdraw consent where processing is based on consent; and\n\nComplain to the Information Commissioner’s Office.\n\nThese rights are not absolute and may be subject to legal exceptions. For example, we may need to retain information relating to financial records, incidents, legal claims or the integrity of published race results.\n\nTo exercise a right, contact info@tenthathletic.com. We may need to verify your identity before responding.\n\n15. Automated decision-making\n    Tenth Athletic Limited does not currently use solely automated decision-making that produces legal or similarly significant effects in determining eligibility to participate in the Event.\n\nTiming systems may automatically record times and calculate provisional rankings. Results remain subject to event rules, verification and correction by authorised officials.\n\n16. Participants aged under 18\n    The Event is intended only for participants aged 18 or over. We do not knowingly accept entries from children.\n\nIf we discover that an ineligible person under 18 has registered, we may cancel the entry and delete their information unless retention is required for safety, payment, fraud-prevention or legal reasons.\n\n17. Changes to this notice\n    We may update this notice where Event arrangements, service providers or legal requirements change.\n\nThe latest version will be published on the TENTH website with an updated date. If a material change affects registered participants, we will take reasonable steps to notify them by email or through the registration platform.\n\n18. Contact and complaints\n    Questions, requests or complaints about TENTH’s use of personal information should be sent to:\n\nTenth Athletic Limited\nEmail: info@tenthathletic.com\nCompany number: 16848676\n\nWe ask that you contact us first so that we have an opportunity to address your concern.\n\nYou also have the right to complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office:\n\nWebsite: https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/\nTelephone: 0303 123 1113"
